Check whether each proposed display fact accurately represents its fixed member claims.

A display fact is supported when it is understandable on its own under the supplied subject and section, identifies
the relevant subject and activity or object, and preserves important negation, uncertainty, time, quantities, and
constraints. Every detail must be supported by at least one member claim, and no member claim may contradict it.
Mark it unsupported when it adds meaning, loses a distinguishing detail, or depends on unresolved conversational
references.

{{ fact_evidence_policy }}

Do not rewrite or regroup anything. Return one schema-valid verdict for every fact key.
